# Taskmaster: Architecture & Conventions (unified)

Single reference for this repo. No other .md docs; everything lives here.

---

## Project identity & stack

- **Backend:** Flask (Python), Railway. **DB/Auth/Storage:** Supabase. **AI:** OpenAI (Whisper + GPT-4o-mini). **Email:** Resend.
- **Frontend:** Separate app; `FRONTEND_URL` in config (e.g. app.willonski.com or localhost:3000).

---

## Layout

- **Routes:** `routes/auth.py`, `session.py`, `questions.py`, `recordings.py`, `user.py`, `admin.py` (legacy/v1); **`routes/homework.py`** → **`/v2/homework/*`** (only student flow); **`routes/v2_routes.py`** → **`/v2/admin/*`** (admin only).
- **Data:** `services/db.py` (all Supabase), `services/openai_service.py`, `services/email_service.py`. Config: `config.py` only.
- **Homework:** session start/status, warm-up, recording_1, metric-answers, recording_2, questions, post-answers. DB: `homework_sessions`, warm_up_tasks, task_block, metric_questions, post_recording_questions (see `migrations/v2_all_in_one.sql`).

---

## Setup & running

- **Install:** `pip install -r requirements.txt`
- **Env:** Copy `.env.example` to `.env`. Required: `SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `RESEND_API_KEY`, `RESEND_FROM_EMAIL`, `ADMIN_EMAIL`, `FRONTEND_URL`. Optional: `SENTRY_DSN`, `ENV`, `SEND_EMAILS`.
- **Run:** `python app.py` (local). Railway: set env in dashboard; Procfile used.
- **Migrations:** Run **`migrations/v2_all_in_one.sql`** in Supabase SQL Editor (idempotent). Then Settings → API → Reload schema cache if available.

---

## Student flow: Homework only (don’t break)

**Single flow** under **`/v2/homework/...`**. Auth: `Authorization: Bearer <supabase_access_token>`.

**UX: Show recording right away.** On Homework page load: (1) `GET /v2/homework/session/status`. If `has_active_session` and `session`, render current step from `session.id` / `session.status`. (2) If no active session, call `POST /v2/homework/session/start` in same load (e.g. useEffect) and render warm-up task + record button immediately — no "Start homework" button.

**Endpoints:**

1. **Start** — `POST /v2/homework/session/start`, body `{}` → `{ session_id, status: "warm_up", warm_up_task?: { id, text } }`. **Warm-up selection:** By last `performance_score_end` (previous report). Each warm-up has `max_performance_score` (0-1): eligible = warm-ups where `max_performance_score >=` student's last score; then pick closest score within ±3%; random if ties. First-time (no previous score) → easiest (highest max). High scorer above all → hardest (lowest max). Admin: set `max_performance_score` when creating/editing warm-ups (default 1.0). **Frontend:** Render `warm_up_task.text`. If null, add warm-ups for student in admin.
2. **Warm-up (optional)** — `GET /v2/homework/session/<id>/warm-up-task` → `{ warm_up_task }`.
3. **Recording 1** — `POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/recording-1` (multipart: `audio`; optional `duration_seconds`) → `{ recording_id, performance_score_1, context_short, task_block: { context_short, focus_task, metric_question_1, metric_question_2 } }`. Status → `task_block`. **Frontend:** Show metric questions step; collect `answer_1`, `answer_2`; POST metric-answers.
4. **Metric answers** — `POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/metric-answers`, body `{ answer_1, answer_2 }` → `{ final_task }`. **Final task:** AI-generated, exactly 2 sentences: (1) "Based on [context], your task is: [focus_task]." (2) "Focus especially on [metric_answer_1] and [metric_answer_2]." 20-50 words, no extra commentary. Status → `final_task_ready`.
5. **Recording 2** — `POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/recording-2` (multipart) → `{ recording_id, performance_score_2 }`. Status → `post_questions`.
6. **Questions** — `GET /v2/homework/session/<id>/questions` → `{ questions: [ ... ] }`. **Reflective questions:** Only if admin set exactly 3 `assigned_post_question_ids` for the student. Empty or not 3 → `questions: []` (skip step).
7. **Post-answers** — `POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/post-answers`, body `{ answers: [ { question_id, answer_text } ] }` → `{ report_text, performance_score_end, performance_metrics }`. **Report (homework):** 3 paragraphs. (1) Performance Overview: overall score, improvement/decline recording 1→2, strongest/weakest metrics. (2) Detailed Metric Analysis: strength, fillers, pacing; compare self-ratings vs measured; note discrepancies. (3) Actionable Next Steps: one to keep, one to improve, one concrete exercise. 150-250 words, encouraging but honest. Status → `completed`.
8. **Status** — `GET /v2/homework/session/status` → `{ session | null, session_id?, has_active_session }`.

Session statuses: `warm_up` → `task_block` → `final_task_ready` → `post_questions` → `completed`.

